WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.004 --> 00:00:03.684
"Rise and shine!"

2
00:00:03.964 --> 00:00:05.145
the computer announced.

3
00:00:05.725 --> 00:00:07.705
"It's time to get up!"

4
00:00:09.586 --> 00:00:10.206
Ally yawned.

5
00:00:10.226 --> 00:00:32.852
"And you know that means," the computer continued.

6
00:00:32.872 --> 00:00:39.334
"I sure do, Alpha," Ally said as the computer's lights started blinking and dance music blared from speakers.

7
00:00:39.354 --> 00:00:41.995
"Dance party!"

8
00:00:42.355 --> 00:00:43.135
the computer said.

9
00:00:43.575 --> 00:00:45.736
Ally leaped out of bed and danced around the pod.

10
00:00:45.756 --> 00:00:51.217
"Do the Kleptorian twist," the computer called out.

11
00:00:51.837 --> 00:00:53.258
Ally did a twisty dance move.

12
00:00:53.278 --> 00:00:56.999
"Now the Jardonian tango."

13
00:00:59.599 --> 00:01:01.400
Ally laughed as she changed up her moves.

14
00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:04.129
"I love starting the day this way!"

15
00:01:04.149 --> 00:01:11.013
"Evidence indicates that dancing is excellent for waking up the Astralian brain and body," the computer said.

16
00:01:11.894 --> 00:01:14.616
Ally danced over to a storage hatch and removed a small box.

17
00:01:16.116 --> 00:01:17.097
She placed it on the table.

18
00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:21.260
"You can turn off the music now," she said.

19
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.502
"I'm wide awake and ready to count my money."

20
00:01:25.262 --> 00:01:27.864
The computer fell silent as Ally pulled money out of the box.

21
00:01:28.668 --> 00:01:32.831
Using her superior mathematic abilities, she flipped through the bills and added them up in just a few

22
00:01:32.871 --> 00:01:38.415
seconds. "Eight hundred and thirty-five," she said.

23
00:01:38.435 --> 00:01:42.598
"This is more than enough to buy the parts and fuel we need to get back home.

24
00:01:43.418 --> 00:01:47.261
I never thought I'd say this, Alpha, but I can't wait to see my parents.

25
00:01:48.522 --> 00:01:50.563
Can you tell me exactly what I need to buy?"

26
00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:52.765
The computer's lights flashed.

27
00:01:52.785 --> 00:01:56.968
"Printing out a list of parts and the exact weight of the fuel cells."

28
00:01:58.152 --> 00:01:59.192
Ally grabbed the printout.

29
00:01:59.212 --> 00:02:03.714
"Great! Now I need to find the time to go buy everything.

30
00:02:04.254 --> 00:02:07.555
Ever since the diner reopened, I haven't had any time off."

31
00:02:12.856 --> 00:02:17.617
When Ally got to the diner, Randy, a new assistant cook, was grilling in the kitchen while Mateo

32
00:02:17.677 --> 00:02:18.738
ate breakfast at the counter.

33
00:02:19.398 --> 00:02:20.838
His face was buried in his phone.

34
00:02:20.858 --> 00:02:24.839
"Texting with Bethany again?"

35
00:02:25.239 --> 00:02:25.840
Ally teased.

36
00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.180
Mateo blushed.

37
00:02:29.337 --> 00:02:32.819
"We're making plans to go to the sci-fi convention on Friday.

38
00:02:33.499 --> 00:02:34.680
You're coming with us, right?"

39
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.782
"Do you always ask others to join your dates?"

40
00:02:39.242 --> 00:02:41.804
Ally asked.

41
00:02:41.824 --> 00:02:44.305
"No Mateo gave her a funny look.

42
00:02:44.325 --> 00:02:48.067
"It's kind of a group thing—Kate is coming.

43
00:02:48.687 --> 00:02:50.228
And the convention is really fun.

44
00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:55.251
It's got rides, an alien costume contest, and cool exhibits."

45
00:02:56.412 --> 00:02:59.209
"Um, I'll think about it," Ally said quickly.

46
00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.192
She couldn't tell Mateo, but she planned to be gone by Friday.

47
00:03:03.552 --> 00:03:04.673
She felt a sharp pang.

48
00:03:04.693 --> 00:03:08.175
"I'm really going to miss him," she thought.

49
00:03:09.796 --> 00:03:12.518
Ally was relieved when Ray called her into the office a second later.

50
00:03:12.939 --> 00:03:14.680
She didn't want Mateo to see her teary-eyed.

51
00:03:19.163 --> 00:03:20.784
morning, Ray," Ally said.

52
00:03:20.804 --> 00:03:23.085
"Ready for another busy day?"

53
00:03:23.105 --> 00:03:27.408
"Yes, especially since I have Randy helping in the kitchen," Ray said.

54
00:03:27.428 --> 00:03:30.169
"Now we have to hire more waitstaff to help you.

55
00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:31.890
Can you help out with the interviews?

56
00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:33.870
You know the job better than anyone."

57
00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.651
"No problem," Ally said.

58
00:03:37.311 --> 00:03:39.112
She was secretly glad Ray had asked her.

59
00:03:39.472 --> 00:03:42.173
Now she could be sure that Ray had great help after she was gone.

60
00:03:42.753 --> 00:03:46.654
As Ally turned to leave the office, she noticed Ray staring at the photo on his desk again.

61
00:03:46.674 --> 00:03:50.535
"I don't want to read his mind," she thought.

62
00:03:50.555 --> 00:03:53.176
"It feels wrong for something so personal.

63
00:03:53.644 --> 00:03:57.427
But why does he always look so sad when he stares at that photo?"

64
00:03:59.488 --> 00:04:03.571
Ally interviewed job candidates all day long, although she kept thinking of it as inner-viewing.

65
00:04:04.072 --> 00:04:07.894
She read all the candidates' minds to see who had the nicest thoughts about the diner and working

66
00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:08.335
for Ray.

67
00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:12.958
"Ray needs people who will really care about the job," Ally thought.

68
00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.002
She was relieved when she interviewed a woman named Flo.

69
00:04:18.442 --> 00:04:20.664
Flo had lots of experience working in busy diners.

70
00:04:21.492 --> 00:04:24.174
"I just love serving good food to people!"

71
00:04:24.615 --> 00:04:25.035
she said.

72
00:04:25.736 --> 00:04:27.998
Flo also loved the new space theme at Ray's Diner.

73
00:04:29.319 --> 00:04:32.081
After Ally talked to Ray, he decided to hire Flo on the spot.

74
00:04:33.462 --> 00:04:34.183
Ally grinned.

75
00:04:34.203 --> 00:04:39.107
"If I train her today, I can take tomorrow morning off to go shopping," she thought.

76
00:04:39.127 --> 00:04:42.189
"This is working out great for everyone!"

77
00:04:44.031 --> 00:04:46.573
The last interview of the day was with a teenager named Barry.

78
00:04:46.593 --> 00:04:48.435
"I hope you'll hire me!"

79
00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:49.756
Barry said eagerly.

80
00:04:50.548 --> 00:04:52.930
"Ray's Diner is so unique and successful!"

81
00:04:53.951 --> 00:04:57.233
When Ally read his mind, she could see that Barry desperately wanted the job.

82
00:04:57.253 --> 00:05:03.758
"Wow," Ally thought, "getting this job means so much to him."

83
00:05:04.438 --> 00:05:05.459
Just then Ray came over.

84
00:05:05.479 --> 00:05:07.460
"I love your enthusiasm, Barry.

85
00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:13.504
You're Barry whooped and ran out of the diner.

86
00:05:16.587 --> 00:05:18.228
Ally and Ray looked at each other and laughed.

87
00:05:19.258 --> 00:05:21.670
"I guess that means he'll take the job!"

88
00:05:22.032 --> 00:05:22.474
Ally said.
